ate on screen. I didn't run the Python checks (`ruff`, `pytest`) because the change is frontend-only.\n\n- **Status pill:** it reads \"Watcher stopped\" with a warn-coloured dot, and its panel shows the stopped sentence in place of the watching / not-watching paragraph.\n- **Live page:** the stopped callout appears first in the opening-hand, intermission and in-match branches. The no-match branch uses `watcherCallout(live.data)`, so it shows the stopped sentence when relevant and the not-watching one otherwise.\n- **Home first run:** the first step's detail is `watcherCallout(live) ?? NOT_WATCHING_SENTENCE`. `STEPS` is now a function of `live`.\n- **`lib/home.ts`:** I added `WATCHER_STOPPED_SENTENCE`, `watcherCallout`, and `liveState` with its `LiveState` type, as the spec describes.\n\nI didn't commit anything.", "ttft_ms": 2155, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 33034, "uuid": "c4aae081-a716-48ee-bf2a-c8eb4b2e7677", "ttft_stream_ms": 1441, "time_to_request_ms": 110, "first_content_frame_ms": 1442, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
